## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design memory pressure handling at the container scale, considering NUMA topology, page migration, and I/O overlap with computation.

## Key Concepts

- Per-container quotas enforced via cgroups memory controller
- NUMA-aware page migration and compaction targeting node-local memory
- Coordination with page fault handler and writeback daemon
- Fairness under contention using weight-based throttling and steal tracking

## Code Example

